- optimize codebook list (section_data): still greedy per-band choice, no
  joint/DP optimization across section boundaries (huff2.c writebooks)
- optimize CPE windows grouping: block-switch decision still per-channel,
  not joint across the pair (blockswitch.c)
- Add bit reservoir control: only a fixed end-of-frame padding calc exists
  today (bitstream.c), no adaptive bit-spend/borrow
- Test TNS(arcen, Apr 8th, 2012): tuned extensively (whitening gate,
  short-window+TD gate, low-bitrate music) and found net-negative on the
  49-clip ViSQOL corpus in every variant tried; kept disabled by default
- add PCE (Program Config Element) or 4-bit AudioSpecificConfig

HE-AAC v1 follow-ups:
(shared signal detector shipped as sbr_analysis.c, feeding block-switch and
SBR numEnvelopes; wiring it to the TNS whitening gate was tried and dropped,
no MOS gain over the fixed 1.4 LC default)
- SBR noise floor / invf mode from tonality (now fixed 4 / 3): a spectral-
  flatness-based attempt was net-negative; needs a within-band/temporal
  tonality measure instead
- SBR envelope border at the transient: VARFIX is selected on transients
  (sbr_adopt_envelope_grid), but numEnvelopes/eff_amp_res/tEnv live in
  SBRInfo (frame-global, shared by both CPE channels); move to SBRChannel
  for independent per-channel borders
- write_sbr_noise: use dedicated noise Huffman tables (blocked on
  numNoiseBands hardcoded to 1 in sbr.c)
- attach ISO 14496-3 table citations directly to compute_kx/compute_k2
  (file already cites the spec elsewhere in sbr.c, just not on these two)
- add SBR/resample sanity tests
